Third-party codec source notices

rapidgzip / librapidarchive
--------------------------
The minimal header subset in rapidgzip/ originates from
https://github.com/mxmlnkn/indexed_bzip2 at revision
1221a30bb548b305a69e5715f2bc348ba37ac243, used by rapidgzip.
Upstream MIT and Apache license texts are retained in that directory.

SWQC adaptations are not upstream behavior claims:
- Replace host file/thread plumbing with a concrete CPE memory reader and
  direct offset dispatch for relocated CPE text.
- Avoid exception-based normal buffer refill and reject reserved distance
  codes through the decoder status path.
- Adapt diagnostic and constexpr helpers for the Sunway C++ toolchain.
- Bound the stored-block finder's look-behind at input interval boundaries.
- Optionally separate large window/lookup arrays from the hot decoder state
  for LDM placement, without changing DEFLATE semantics.

The first-pass scheduler, runtime integration, buffer leases and CPE wrappers
outside this vendor directory are SWQC code, not the upstream parallel reader.

zlib
----
The compressor subset in zlib/ originates from https://github.com/madler/zlib
at revision 767c4c947852e143f582c85f14cf573411df1b35.
The upstream license text and source copyright notices are retained.
Local alteration: deflate.c selects the original level/strategy compressor
through equivalent direct calls instead of an immutable function-pointer table,
so calls remain valid after CPE text relocation. Unused inflate implementation
files are omitted; the MPE uses system zlib for the serial decoder/fallback.

Compression follows pigz's ordered raw-DEFLATE fragment composition with a
preceding 32 KiB dictionary. It uses zlib CPE jobs, not pigz's POSIX worker pool.
